IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-definitions`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, sections 95 to 97 -- THE RECORD OF EARNINGS.
-- Piece cp6, lines 2653 to 2676 of the Act file.
--
-- Section 95 makes the Minister keep the Record of Earnings. Section 96 lets a contributor ask for a
-- statement of what the Record shows to the contributor's account and ask the Minister to reconsider it.
-- Section 97 makes an entry in the Record final four years after the end of the year it was made in,
-- and says when the Minister may nonetheless rectify the Record, remove an entry, or reduce a
-- contributor's earnings, and what the contributor is then owed.
--
-- THE JURAL RELATIONS (written once each, named neutrally; NOTES.md has the table):
--   s 95      the Minister's duty to keep the Record. The text names no one who may demand it.
--   s 96(1)   a contributor's power to require a statement, and the Minister's liability to furnish it;
--             a contributor's power to ask for reconsideration, and the Minister's liability to reconsider.
--   s 97(1)   a contributor's disability to question an entry after four years (the Minister's immunity).
--   s 97(2)   the Minister's power to rectify upwards, the contributor's liability to it (a gain).
--   s 97(2.1) the Minister's power to remove an entry, the contributor's liability to it.
--   s 97(3)   the Minister's power to reduce another contributor's earnings, that contributor's liability.
--   s 97(4)   the Minister's duty to notify a reduction, the contributor's claim to be told; the contributor's
--             power to ask for reconsideration of the reduction.
--
-- WHAT THE MODULE TAKES AS INPUTS, NOT AS RULES. Whether a person is a contributor is the core's section 2(1)
-- rule (cpp-core-definitions.l4); the four facts it turns on are carried in one record below. "The prescribed
-- manner" of applying under s 96(1) and of notifying under s 97(4) is regulation 39 and regulation 40 (piece
-- cr2); each is taken here as a plain yes/no input, passed through the core's section 2(1) "prescribed".
-- Sections 81 and 82 (reconsideration and appeal, piece cp5) are applied, not reproduced.
--
-- FORKS (NOTES.md, fork register): C6-F1 where s 95's "and" between its three purposes joins them;
-- C6-F2 whether the last day of the four years is still open; C6-F3 the effect of an agreement under s 105 on s 96(1);
-- C6-F4 s 97(2.1) refers to "paragraph 105(1)(a)" and section 105 has no subsection (1).

§ `Part III -- the Record of Earnings (sections 95 to 97)`

§§ `The facts that make a person a contributor`

-- Not a provision: carries the four facts of section 2(1) "contributor" so that every rule of this module
-- can be asked of one person with one argument. The core's own rule decides the term.
-- out of range: subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i) and sections 55, 55.1 and 55.2 (piece cp3). The facts are plain inputs; the core's section 2(1) decides who is a contributor.
DECLARE `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor` HAS
    `the person has made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
    `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS A BOOLEAN

-- Not a provision: asks the core's section 2(1) "contributor" rule about one person.
GIVEN facts IS A `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` facts MEANS
    `s 2(1) — a contributor`
        (facts's `the person has made an employee's contribution`)
        (facts's `the person has made a contribution on the person's own self-employed earnings`)
        (facts's `the person's earnings on which a contribution was made, for each year, as in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)`)
        (facts's `earnings have been attributed to the person under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2`)

§§ `Section 95 -- the Record of Earnings`

-- src:2654 | Record of Earnings
-- src:2655 | 95 The Minister shall cause to be established such records, to be known as the Record of Earnings, of information obtained under this Act with respect to the earnings and contributions of contributors, including information obtained pursuant to any agreement entered into under section 105 with respect to those earnings and contributions, as are necessary to permit
-- src:2656 | (a) the determination of the amount of any benefit that may be payable under this Act to or in respect of any contributor;
-- src:2657 | (b) the calculation of the amount of any financial adjustment that may be required to be made pursuant to any agreement entered into under subsection 80(1); and
-- src:2658 | (c) the identification of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of contributors, according to information contained in returns made pursuant to Part I.
-- out of range: subsection 80(1) (piece cp5): whether an agreement under it needs the information is a plain input.
@ref Act s 95 (src:2654-2658)
GIVEN `the information was obtained under this Act, including under an agreement under section 105` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is about the earnings and contributions of contributors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary to permit the determination of a benefit payable to or in respect of a contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary to permit the calculation of a financial adjustment under an agreement under subsection 80(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary to permit the identification of unadjusted pensionable earnings from returns made under Part I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 95 — the information is to be kept in the Record of Earnings` `the information was obtained under this Act, including under an agreement under section 105` `the information is about the earnings and contributions of contributors` `the information is necessary to permit the determination of a benefit payable to or in respect of a contributor` `the information is necessary to permit the calculation of a financial adjustment under an agreement under subsection 80(1)` `the information is necessary to permit the identification of unadjusted pensionable earnings from returns made under Part I` MEANS
        `the information was obtained under this Act, including under an agreement under section 105`
    AND `the information is about the earnings and contributions of contributors`
    -- "as are necessary to permit (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ...": read as alternatives (fork C6-F1), because the Record
    -- is the whole body of records that makes all three purposes possible.
    AND (   `the information is necessary to permit the determination of a benefit payable to or in respect of a contributor`
         OR `the information is necessary to permit the calculation of a financial adjustment under an agreement under subsection 80(1)`
         OR `the information is necessary to permit the identification of unadjusted pensionable earnings from returns made under Part I`)

§§ `Section 96 -- the statement of earnings, and a request for reconsideration`

-- NOTHING means that an agreement under section 105 governs the case and the agreement is not among the texts
-- this encoding reads (fork C6-F3): the Act alone does not decide.
-- src:2659 | Application for statement of earnings and request for reconsideration
-- src:2660 | 96 (1) Subject to the provisions of any agreement entered into under section 105, every contributor may require the Minister, by application made in the prescribed manner, to furnish or make available to the contributor a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor’s account in the Record of Earnings, and if a contributor is not satisfied with the statement, they may request that it be reconsidered by the Minister.
@ref Act s 96(1) (src:2659-2660)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor`
      `the application is made in the manner a regulation prescribes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) — a contributor's application obliges the Minister to furnish a statement of the unadjusted pensionable earnings` facts `the application is made in the manner a regulation prescribes` `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor` MEANS
    IF `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` facts
               -- "in the prescribed manner": section 2(1) "prescribed", any other matter (regulation 39, piece cr2)
               AND `s 2(1) — prescribed` `any other matter` FALSE `the application is made in the manner a regulation prescribes` FALSE)

@ref Act s 96(1) (src:2659-2660)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp6 Facts that make a person a contributor`
      `the Minister has furnished the contributor a statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor is not satisfied with the statement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 96(1) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the statement` facts `the Minister has furnished the contributor a statement` `the contributor is not satisfied with the statement` `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor` MEANS
    IF `an agreement under section 105 governs how the statement is made available to the contributor`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (    `a person described by facts is a contributor under section 2(1)` facts
               AND `the Minister has furnished the contributor a statement`
               AND `the contributor is not satisfied with the statement`)

-- src:2661 | Application of sections 81 and 82
-- src:2662 | (2) Sections 81 and 82 apply with any modifications that the circumstances require to any request made under subsection (1) as though it were an application for a benefit.
@ref Act s 96(2) (src:2661-2662)
GIVEN `the request is made under subsection 96(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 96(2) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` `the request is made under subsection 96(1)` MEANS
    -- "with any modifications that the circumstances require": the modifications are not stated, so none is encoded.
    -- Sections 81 and 82 are out of range: section 81 and 82 (piece cp5).
    `the request is made under subsection 96(1)`

-- src:2663 | (3) [Repealed, 1995, c. 33, s. 40]
-- Subsection 96(3) is repealed in this text and states nothing.

§§ `Section 97 -- an entry in the Record is presumed accurate; rectification`

-- Counted as the core counts a year (section 2(1) "year": 1 January to 31 December). The end of the year in
-- which the entry was made is its last day; four years from that day is 31 December four years later.
-- src:2664 | Entry in record of earnings presumed to be accurate
-- src:2665 | 97 (1) Notwithstanding section 96, except as provided in this section, any entry in the Record of Earnings relating to the earnings or a contribution of a contributor shall be conclusively presumed to be accurate and may not be called into question after four years have elapsed from the end of the year in which the entry was made.
@ref Act s 97(1) (src:2664-2665)
GIVEN `year in which the entry was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` `year in which the entry was made` MEANS
    -- Fork C6-F2: "after four years have elapsed from the end of the year": the four years are complete at the
    -- close of 31 December of the fourth year after, and the entry may still be questioned on that day.
    `the date a time limit ends` (`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` `year in which the entry was made`) (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 4)

@ref Act s 97(1) (src:2664-2665)
GIVEN `year in which the entry was made` IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` `year in which the entry was made` day MEANS
    day AT MOST (`s 97(1) — the last day on which an entry may be called into question` `year in which the entry was made`)

-- "conclusively presumed to be accurate": from the first day after the four years the entry cannot be called
-- into question, whatever the facts. The Minister's powers in subsections (2), (2.1) and (3) are the
-- "except as provided in this section" and carry no time limit, so they are not touched by this rule.
@ref Act s 97(1) (src:2664-2665)
GIVEN `year in which the entry was made` IS A NUMBER
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(1) — an entry is conclusively presumed to be accurate on a day` `year in which the entry was made` day MEANS
    NOT (`s 97(1) — an entry may be called into question on a day` `year in which the entry was made` day)

-- src:2666 | Rectification of Record in certain cases
-- src:2667 | (2) If
-- src:2668 | (a) from information furnished by or obtained from the records of an employer or a former employer, or an employee or a former employee of an employer, or a person required to make a contribution in respect of this self-employed earnings, after the time specified in subsection (1), or
-- src:2669 | (b) for any other reason,
-- src:2670 | it appears to the Minister that the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown in the Record of Earnings to the account of an employee or former employee of that employer or to the account of that person is less than the amount that should be so shown in that Record, the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified in order to show the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor that should be so shown therein.
@ref Act s 97(2) (src:2666-2670)
GIVEN `the information was furnished by or obtained from the records of an employer, a former employer, an employee, a former employee or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings, after the time specified in subsection 97(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister, for any other reason, that the amount shown is less than the amount that should be shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the account` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount that it appears to the Minister should be shown to the account` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(2) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified upwards` `the information was furnished by or obtained from the records of an employer, a former employer, an employee, a former employee or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings, after the time specified in subsection 97(1)` `it appears to the Minister, for any other reason, that the amount shown is less than the amount that should be shown` `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the account` `the amount that it appears to the Minister should be shown to the account` MEANS
    -- Paragraph (a) is a source of information, paragraph (b) is "any other reason": together they cover every case
    -- in which it appears to the Minister that the amount shown is less than the amount that should be shown.
    -- The judgment "it appears to the Minister" is the Minister's, so it is a conditional input and is never guessed.
        (   `the information was furnished by or obtained from the records of an employer, a former employer, an employee, a former employee or a person required to contribute on self-employed earnings, after the time specified in subsection 97(1)`
         OR `it appears to the Minister, for any other reason, that the amount shown is less than the amount that should be shown`)
    AND `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the account` LESS THAN `the amount that it appears to the Minister should be shown to the account`

-- src:2671 | Removal of entry
-- src:2672 | (2.1) If, from information furnished pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 105(1)(a), it appears to the Minister that an amount that is shown in the Record of Earnings to the account of a person as being a contribution under this Act relates instead to a contribution under the provincial pension plan of that province, the Minister may, at any time after that information is furnished, authorize the removal of that entry from the Record of Earnings.
@ref Act s 97(2.1) (src:2671-2672)
GIVEN `the information was furnished pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 105(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that the amount shown as a contribution under this Act relates instead to a contribution under the provincial pension plan of that province` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the information was furnished` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(2.1) — the Minister may authorize the removal of an entry from the Record of Earnings on a day` `the information was furnished pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 105(a)` `it appears to the Minister that the amount shown as a contribution under this Act relates instead to a contribution under the provincial pension plan of that province` `the day the information was furnished` day MEANS
    -- The text says "paragraph 105(1)(a)"; section 105 has no subsection (1) (fork C6-F4), so paragraph 105(a) is read.
        `the information was furnished pursuant to an agreement referred to in paragraph 105(a)`
    AND `it appears to the Minister that the amount shown as a contribution under this Act relates instead to a contribution under the provincial pension plan of that province`
    -- "at any time after that information is furnished": no end date, so only the start is tested.
    AND day AT LEAST `the day the information was furnished`

-- src:2673 | Idem
-- src:2674 | (3) Where the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor shown to his account in the Record of Earnings is increased pursuant to subsection (2) and it appears to the Minister that the earnings and contributions with respect to which that amount is so increased have been incorrectly shown in the Record to the account of another contributor, the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by reducing the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown in the Record to the account of that other contributor by such part of that amount as has been incorrectly so shown therein.
@ref Act s 97(3) (src:2673-2674)
GIVEN `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the first contributor was increased pursuant to subsection 97(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Minister that the earnings and contributions with respect to which that amount was increased were incorrectly shown to the account of another contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(3) — the Minister may cause the Record of Earnings to be rectified by a reduction of another contributor's earnings` `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the first contributor was increased pursuant to subsection 97(2)` `it appears to the Minister that the earnings and contributions with respect to which that amount was increased were incorrectly shown to the account of another contributor` MEANS
        `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the first contributor was increased pursuant to subsection 97(2)`
    AND `it appears to the Minister that the earnings and contributions with respect to which that amount was increased were incorrectly shown to the account of another contributor`

-- The reduction is "such part of that amount as has been incorrectly so shown". When the Minister makes the
-- rectification, the other contributor's earnings fall by that part; when the Minister does not, they do not.
@ref Act s 97(3) (src:2673-2674)
GIVEN `the Minister rectifies the Record under subsection 97(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor` IS A NUMBER
      `the part of the increase that was incorrectly shown to the other contributor` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 97(3) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor after any reduction` `the Minister rectifies the Record under subsection 97(3)` `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor` `the part of the increase that was incorrectly shown to the other contributor` MEANS
    IF `the Minister rectifies the Record under subsection 97(3)`
    THEN `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor` MINUS `the part of the increase that was incorrectly shown to the other contributor`
    ELSE `the amount of unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the other contributor`

-- src:2675 | Notice of rectification to be given
-- src:2676 | (4) Whenever any reduction is made in the amount of the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor shown to their account in the Record of Earnings, whether under subsection (3) or otherwise, and it appears from the Record of Earnings that before the making of the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount of the earnings shown to their account in the Record of Earnings, the Minister must notify the contributor in prescribed manner of his or her action and if the contributor is not satisfied with the amount of the reduction so made, they may request that such action be reconsidered by the Minister and sections 81 and 82 apply with any modifications that the circumstances require to that request as though it were an application for a benefit.
@ref Act s 97(4) (src:2675-2676)
GIVEN `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(4) — the Minister must notify the contributor of the reduction` `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise` `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown` MEANS
        `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise`
    AND `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown`

-- Whether the notice was given "in prescribed manner" is regulation 40 (piece cr2): in writing, addressed to the
-- contributor's latest known address. It is a yes/no input here.
@ref Act s 97(4) (src:2675-2676)
GIVEN `the Minister notified the contributor in writing at the contributor's latest known address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(4) — the notice of the reduction was given in the prescribed manner` `the Minister notified the contributor in writing at the contributor's latest known address` MEANS
    `s 2(1) — prescribed` `any other matter` FALSE `the Minister notified the contributor in writing at the contributor's latest known address` FALSE

@ref Act s 97(4) (src:2675-2676)
GIVEN `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor is not satisfied with the amount of the reduction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(4) — a contributor's dissatisfaction obliges the Minister to reconsider the reduction` `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise` `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown` `the contributor is not satisfied with the amount of the reduction` MEANS
        `a reduction is made in the unadjusted pensionable earnings shown to the contributor's account, under subsection 97(3) or otherwise`
    AND `it appears from the Record that before the reduction the contributor had been informed under section 96 of the amount shown`
    AND `the contributor is not satisfied with the amount of the reduction`

-- "sections 81 and 82 apply with any modifications that the circumstances require to that request as though
-- it were an application for a benefit". Sections 81 and 82 are out of range: section 81 and 82 (piece cp5).
@ref Act s 97(4) (src:2675-2676)
GIVEN `the request for reconsideration is made under subsection 97(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 97(4) — sections 81 and 82 apply to the request as though it were an application for a benefit` `the request for reconsideration is made under subsection 97(4)` MEANS
    `the request for reconsideration is made under subsection 97(4)`
